[D Forever Druid 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Built 2 Nov 2026 from QuestieDB Forever 1.0.10 and the Wowhead Zephras Isle pull of 2 Nov 2026; step order checked against Polestar 0.2.6 and TUGs.\\Skyborne Druid (feral): Thendal Grove, level 1 to the road south to Shen'dar.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffZephras Isle 1-6|r  -  the Skyborne start in Thendal Grove (Skyborne Druid, feral: Bear Form 10-20, Cat Form from 20). Horde and other-class quests on the island are not in this guide.
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Gear rule:|r leather, cloth where no leather is offered (no mail). Weapon dps first - in Bear and Cat Form your auto-attack hits with your weapon's dps (Blizzard's Forever druid deep dive) - then Str > Sta > Agi in the bear band (10-19) and Str > Agi > Sta from Cat Form at 20. Weights: docs/forever-feral-stat-weights.md (reasoning only, nothing tested in game).
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Fighting 1-9 (Classic reasoning, unverified on Forever):|r keep Mark of the Wild up; pull with Wrath, Moonfire from 4 as the mob closes, then melee with your weapon; Rejuvenation on yourself when hurt, Thorns from 6 before each pull.
[OC]|cffffcc00Professions (Forever):|r |cff66ff66Skinning + Mining first|r, plus First Aid + Cooking + Fishing: two gathering skills that pay gold from level 1 with passives that help a solo character. Passives: Skinning = +5% damage to Beasts and Dragonkin, Mining = +5% total health. There are no profession trainers in Thendal Grove: you learn them on arrival in Shen'dar (6-14 Zephras Isle), except that the Harvesting Windstones reward book below teaches Skinning here.
[OC]|cffffcc00Cooking + Fishing plan (Forever):|r your food ladder is Roasted Boar Meat (+1 Str, trainer) -> |cff66ff66Longjaw Mud Snapper (+10 attack power, level 5+)|r -> |cff66ff66Mithril Head Trout (+20 attack power, level 25+)|r. Both fish come from your own fishing rod, so Fishing is part of this guide: learn it in Shen'dar (6-14 Zephras Isle), buy Khara Deepwater's Strong Fishing Pole (+45 Fishing in Forever) at the loch, and fish where the guide says "fish to N". Skill targets: Cooking 50 by 12 (Journeyman at Daryl Riknussun, Ironforge), 80 by 16, 125 by 24 (Expert Cookbook from Shandrina, Ashenvale), 175 by ~30 for the trout; Fishing 25 by 12, 50 by 15 (Journeyman at Grimnur Stonebrand, Ironforge), 100 by 22, 130+ by 28. Every other recipe on the route is a skill-up filler: cook whatever meat you loot and eat the best thing you have.
[OC]|cffffcc00Camping (Forever):|r Cooking 1 teaches the Basic Campfire (3 object slots). Sit or craft at a fire for 1 minute to get its buffs (1 hour). Each player adds ONE profession object: your Lodestone (Mining 20) = melee attack power, your Camp Chair (Skinning 20) = +2% crit, First Aid Kit = stamina, Fish Bowl (Fishing 20; does not stack with Blessing of Kings) = +8% all stats, Leatherworking tent = rested XP. Objects have a 1-hour cooldown and the fire vanishes after ~10-15 min, so set camp right before a dungeon or a long grind, with your friend adding his object. The Camping 101 quests (level 6, Raan Wildwind outside Shen'dar) teach the tier-1 objects once that skill is 20.
[OC]|cffffcc00Skyborne racials|r (Blizzard's Skyborne post): Walk on Air glides you downward for 10 seconds (two quests here use it), Read Ley Line activates a ley line for +100% health and mana regeneration (one quest here uses it), Wind Blessed +1% haste, Elemental Insight +5% damage to Elementals. Zephras Isle has no inn, hearth or flight master; the tornadoes on the island give +40% run speed for 5 minutes (unverified) - run through them.
[OC]|cffffcc00Launch rule (1-6):|r no shared tags in Forever - on a camped named mob (the Cirrusfly Queen, Urs'anah the Den Mother, Malduko Cloudcrush) INVITE the people standing there (kill credit shares in a party; most drop items don't). If no group forms in ~2 min, tick the step and keep moving; the catch-up line before you leave the grove brings you back. Expect the first 10-20 min to be the worst.

